/addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p> alpha -Agarase having the following physicochemical properties: (1) function: hydrolyzing an  alpha -1,3 bond between 3,6-anhydro-L-galactose and D-galactose; (2) substrate specificity: acting on agarose and agarohexaose and higher agarooligosaccharides but not on agarotetraose; (3) optimum temperature: showing its enzymatic activity at 55  DEG C or below; and (4) heat stability: sustaining 20% or more of the activity after being treated at 48  DEG C for 30 seconds.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une  alpha -agarase présentant les propriétés physico-chimiques suivantes: 1) fonction: hydrolyse une liaison  alpha -1,3 entre la 3,6-anhydro-L-galactose et la D-galactose; 2) spécificité de substrat: agit sur l'agarose et l'agarohexaose et des agaro-oligosaccharides supérieurs mais pas sur l'agarotétraose; 3) température optimale: activité enzymatique à une température égale ou inférieure à 55  DEG C; et 4) stabilité à la chaleur: conserve un taux d'activité égal ou supérieur à 20 % après traitement à 48  DEG C pendant 30 secondes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>